    {"role": "user", "content": "So the system must be one where no external forces act on it?"},
    {"role": "assistant", "reasoning": "The learner correctly identifies that no external forces must act on the system. This is the key condition. I should confirm this and then guide them to the second missing word — the word that describes the momentum being conserved. The memo says 'total linear momentum'. I'll ask them what word describes the momentum of the whole system.", "content": "Yes, exactly right! ✅ When no external forces act on the system, the momentum stays the same.\n\nNow, the second part of the statement. When we talk about momentum being conserved, we're talking about the momentum of the whole system — all the objects together. What word would you use to describe the momentum of the entire system, as opposed to just one object?"}
  ],
